<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates largely softer.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates largely softer.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were largely softer on Tuesday with only the two-week and three-month rates steady, traders said.</p>
<p>The lowering of the Central Bank's overnight rates prompted many banks to lower their swap rates, they said.</p>
<p>The Central Bank had cut its overnight borrowing rate to 10.4375 from 10.5 percent; and its overnight lending to 12.9375 from 13.0 percent.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  MARCH 4		 MARCH 3</p>
<p>    1 W		9  5/8		  9 11/16</p>
<p>    2 W		9  5/8		  9  5/8</p>
<p>    1 M		9  5/8		  9  3/4</p>
<p>    2 M		9 13/16		 9  7/8</p>
<p>    3 M		9  7/8		  9  7/8</p>
<p>    6 M		10			10  1/16</p>
<p>    12M		10  1/4		 10  5/16</p>
<p>    VAL		5-Mar		   4-Mar</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
